# YOLOE Integration into AlgorithmSDK — Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox () syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Make AlgorithmSDK support YOLOE (open-vocabulary YOLO) models by making class names and input size configurable via per-model YAML files, eliminating all hardcoded assumptions that prevent custom/vocabulary-varied models from working.

**Architecture:** Approach A — Minimal config-driven approach. YOLOE ONNX models (after fuse()) produce standard-format output identical to regular YOLO: [1, 300, 6] for detection, [1, 300, 38] + [1, 32, 160, 160] for segmentation. Therefore no new TaskType is needed. Instead, we fix the foundational problem that blocks ANY custom model: hardcoded class names (kClassNames = COCO 80) and hardcoded input size (kInputW/kInputH = 640). These become loaded from a .yaml file that ships alongside each .onnx model. A YOLOE model is then just a DETECT or SEGMENT model with a YAML specifying its vocabulary. This also fixes an existing param-name mismatch bug ("confidence" vs "conf").

**Tech Stack:** C++17, ONNX Runtime C++ API, OpenCV, yaml-cpp, pybind11, CMake

